<title>USA: MTEL Q4 net loss widens.</title>
<headline>MTEL Q4 net loss widens.</headline>
<dateline>JACKSON, Miss. 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>SUMMARY OF OPERATIONS</p>
<p>(All amounts in thousands of dollars except per share amounts)</p>
<p>CONDENSED STATEMENTS OF</p>
<p>OPERATIONS:	     Twelve Months Ended   Three Months Ended</p>
<p>				   December 31,	   December 31,</p>
<p>				 1995	 1996	 1995	1996</p>
<p>Revenues		  $245,991   $350,529   $74,076   $89,727</p>
<p>Operating income (loss) (58,422) (130,947) (41,844)  (68,475)</p>
<p>Net income (loss)    ($52,028) ($171,822) ($40,386) ($82,047)</p>
<p>Net income (loss)</p>
<p>available to common</p>
<p>shareholders	   ($60,465) ($183,417) ($42,495) ($85,286)</p>
<p>Net income (loss) per</p>
<p> common share	    ($1.19)    ($3.38)   ($0.79)   ($1.57)</p>
<p>Weighted average common</p>
<p> shares outstanding     50,812     54,304    54,082    54,400</p>
<p>NOTE: The full company name is Mobile Telecommunication Technologies Corp.</p>
<p>Fourth-quarter operating cash flow, a key paging industry measurement, was $2.5 million compared with negative $24 million in the same quarter of 1995.</p>
<p>One-way operating cash flow was $25.8 million, representing a 33.0 percent operating cash flow margin and a 35 percent increase over fourth quarter 1995 results.</p>
<p>The company said it posted a 1996 Q4 net loss of $43.3 million, or $0.86 per share, prior to a $38.8 million writedown of primarily international development costs.</p>
<p>The 1995 fourth quarter results included an $18.3 million one-time charge from the launch of the company's narrowband PCS network.</p>
